The bug occurs due to improper handling of memory references during disk write operations. The first statement can lead to referencing a page that has been unmapped (`kunmap()`) when incoming data expands on compression. The second statement can cause referencing a buffer that has already been freed (`kfree()`) during partial writes with incompressible data. The third statement sets `user_mem` to a mapped page, which can lead to invalid references if not handled correctly in subsequent operations.

