Reason:
The fix ensures that `kunmap_atomic(user_mem)` is only called when it is safe to do so, specifically when the operation is not a partial I/O. This prevents invalid memory references to unmapped pages. Additionally, the condition for freeing `uncmem` is retained, ensuring that it is only freed when it is allocated for partial I/O, thus preventing references to freed memory.

